            <div id="pnlDepartmentInfo" class="col col-half">
	

                <h3 class="postingHeader">Department Information</h3>

                <div class="postingContent">
		
                    <div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The California Department of Developmental Services (DDS) is the agency through which the State of California provides services and supports to individuals with developmental disabilities.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">These disabilities include intellectual disability, cerebral palsy, epilepsy, autism and related conditions. Services are provided through state-operated developmental centers and community facilities, and contracts with 21 nonprofit regional centers. The regional centers serve as a local resource to help find and access the services and supports available to individuals with developmental disabilities and their families.<br /><br /><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong style="text-decoration-color: initial;">Please direct questions to:&nbsp;</strong></span></span><a href="mailto:CentralValleySTARRecruitment@dds.ca.gov" style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 12pt; text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #0563c1; font-family: Arial; text-decoration-line: underline;">CentralValleySTARRecruitment@dds.ca.gov</span></span></a><a href="mailto:CentralSTARRecruitment@dds.ca.gov" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; color: #800000; text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #0000ff; text-decoration-line: underline;"></span></a></div>
                
	</div>

